The provided class is a thin delegating wrapper around RxJava's Completable infrastructure. Its logic consists only of applying an operator and subscribing to the source, with no computational work of its own. Benchmarking such a trivial pass‑through would not yield meaningful performance insights, as any measured cost would be dominated by the underlying source or operator rather than the `CompletableLift` implementation itself. Therefore, a dedicated JMH benchmark is unnecessary.